    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87-a1">

                <pb facs="0247" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1902app1/pg227"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Division of Appointments.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Treasury Department, Office of the Secretary</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1900-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic">December
                                6, 1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>This is to certify that N. S. Farley and Stanley Jackson were deputy collectors
                    of customs at the port of San Francisco on November 19, 1900, and September 8,
                    1900, respectively, the dates upon which the inclosed papers bearing their
                    signatures were executed, and that they were duly authorized to sign as such
                    officers on the respective dates above named, the signatures appearing thereon
                    being identical with those attached to official papers in the files of this
                    office.</p>
                <closer>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal.</hi>] <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Gage</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
